edit('P0622-Q03',['G3=∂U/∂d3=−(m3+m4)g because upward height decreases as downward d3 increases','G3=−∂U/∂d3, so the displayed negative sign follows from the physical force rather than the left-side gravity term','G3 is obtained by differentiating U with respect to d1 while keeping d3 fixed','G3 is negative because gravitational potential itself must be negative below the arm plane'],['For the convention τ=Mq̈+V+G, the gravity vector is the gradient of potential with respect to the generalized coordinates; z=d1−d3 gives the negative derivative.','The physical generalized gravity force is −∂U/∂d3; the G term placed on the left uses +∂U/∂d3.','The generalized coordinate is d3; fixed base height d1 is not the differentiated joint coordinate.','Potential can be shifted by an arbitrary constant; its derivative, not its absolute sign, determines G3.'])
q=edit('P0623-Q01',['Acceleration: θ=t²; cruise: θ=1+2(t−1); deceleration: θ=6−(4−t)²','Acceleration: θ=t²; cruise: θ=1+2t; deceleration: θ=6−(4−t)²','Acceleration: θ=t²; cruise: θ=1+2(t−1); deceleration: θ=6+(4−t)²','Acceleration: θ=t²; cruise: θ=1+2(t−1); deceleration: θ=6−t²'],['The ramp reaches θa=1 rad and speed 2 rad/s at t=1 s. Cruise measures time from that switch, and the final phase measures time remaining until t=4 s, approaching 6 rad from below.','The cruise expression must use t−1; using t makes position jump from 1 to 3 rad at the first switch.','The plus sign approaches the endpoint from above with negative velocity, contrary to the positive rest-to-rest move.','Using t rather than 4−t loses the terminal reference; it does not give θ(4)=6 rad or zero final speed.'],stem='Use a consistent hypothetical positive rest-to-rest trapezoidal move, not the infeasible numeric table: θ0=0 rad, acceleration magnitude α=2 rad/s², ramp duration ta=1 s, cruise speed vp=2 rad/s, final time T=4 s and θf=6 rad. Which ordered position expressions match acceleration on 0≤t≤1, cruise on 1≤t≤3 and deceleration on 3≤t≤4? Treat t as its numerical value in seconds and each expression as radians.',difficulty='medium',type='numerical',cognitiveSkill='numerical',assumptions=['Symmetric constant acceleration and deceleration; initial and final speeds zero; cruise lasts 2 s. The supplied hypothetical values replace, rather than silently repair, the printed example.'],steps=['Acceleration gives θa=αta²/2=1 rad and vp=αta=2 rad/s.','Cruise position is θa+vp(t−ta)=1+2(t−1), reaching 5 rad at t=3 s.','Deceleration position is θf−α(T−t)²/2=6−(4−t)², joining 5 rad at t=3 and ending at 6 rad with zero speed.'],formulas=copy.deepcopy(qm[B+'-P0623-Q06']['solution']['formulas']))
